# Platform MCP assets — industry alignment

## Config file (what we store under `agent-assets/mcp/*.json`)

Match Cursor / Claude Code / Claude Desktop: **connection only**.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "server-key": {
      "url": "https://…",
      "transport": "sse",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${USER_API_KEY}" }
    }
  }
}
```

- Server **name** = object key under `mcpServers` (not a separate `name` / `id` field).
- Do **not** put `title`, `description`, or `allowTools` in this JSON.
- Catalog title/description live in `agent-assets/manifest.yaml`.
- Tool allowlists (if needed) live on the **agent** (`agent.yaml` → `mcp[].allowTools` or future studio agent policy), not on the MCP asset.
- Stdio `command`/`args`/`env` is the other industry shape; Flue currently supports **remote URL** MCP only.

## UI

- Show connection JSON as the industry-shaped `{ "mcpServers": … }` blob.
- Show **tool chips from runtime discovery** after connect (like Cursor Tools & MCPs), not from static config.
- If credentials are missing, say so — do not invent a tool list in the JSON file.
